From: swibrow <15628653+swibrow@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 05:51:17 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/7] Scan /proc for GPU holders instead of running fuser

With PassthroughSupport enabled, WaitForGPUFree runs
'chroot <host-root> fuser <driver-root>/dev/nvidiaN' before rebinding a
GPU to vfio-pci. On hosts without fuser (e.g. Talos Linux) chroot exits
127 on every attempt, so the check loops until gpuFreeCheckTimeout and
NodePrepareResources fails.

Replace the fuser call with a scan of /proc/<pid>/fd in the host PID
namespace (mounted at /proc when PassthroughSupport is enabled) for
character devices matching the GPU's major:minor. This needs no host
binary, also catches containerized clients that have their own device
nodes, and names the holding processes as <pid>(<exe>) in the error.

Signed-off-by: swibrow <15628653+swibrow@users.noreply.github.com>
(cherry picked from commit 8cbd603e42969d2ef44ef3a13683220ed65232c8)
